From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 19:05:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] media: cedrus: vc1: increase MV buffer size to 112KB
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The vendor allocates 112KB (7×16KB slots) for the motion-vector
workspace. 64KB is marginal for 1920×1080 interlaced-field content
and may overflow, corrupting the adjacent ACDC coefficient buffer.

Match the vendor size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>

[Ported to the VC-1 stateless uAPI revision 3 (gus bourg):
 - MV buffer size and "timestamp 0 = no reference": unchanged.
 - The second-field override used the picture type which the first field
   had saved in the capture buffer; it now uses FPTYPE (I/I or I/P).
   It is also limited to second fields with NUMREF == 0 and
   REFFIELD == 0, i.e. those which can only refer to the first field:
   in this uAPI forward_ref_ts of a second field names the previous
   reference frame on purpose, which a P field with NUMREF == 1 or
   REFFIELD == 1 does use.
 - Not carried over: enabling CEDRUS_VC1_DEBUG and the debug print
   (removed again by "BITS_LEN from slice bit_size"), and taking the raw
   bits from raw_coding_flags (reverted by the same patch: the hardware
   wants the raw bit of every plane which is not passed decoded).]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c   | 26 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
index 816816ff3..bedb5cbcc 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
 #include "cedrus_hw.h"
 #include "cedrus_regs.h"
 
-#define MV_BUF_SIZE			(64 * SZ_1K)
+#define MV_BUF_SIZE			(112 * SZ_1K)
 #define ACDC_BUF_SIZE			(16 * SZ_1K)
 #define BITPLANES_BUF_SIZE		(16 * SZ_1K)
 
@@ -228,8 +228,28 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 
 	vq = v4l2_m2m_get_vq(ctx->fh.m2m_ctx, V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE);
 
-	forward_vb2 = vb2_find_buffer(vq, picture->forward_ref_ts);
-	backward_vb2 = vb2_find_buffer(vq, picture->backward_ref_ts);
+	/*
+	 * For interlaced-field frames whose first field is intra-coded, the
+	 * second field references the first field of the same frame. When
+	 * the bitstream cannot refer to anything else (one reference field,
+	 * the most recent one), point the hardware at the frame being decoded
+	 * rather than at the previous reference frame. A timestamp of 0 means
+	 * no reference.
+	 */
+	if (second_field &&
+	    (picture->fptype == V4L2_VC1_FPTYPE_I_I ||
+	     picture->fptype == V4L2_VC1_FPTYPE_I_P) &&
+	    !(picture->flags & (V4L2_VC1_PICTURE_LAYER_FLAG_NUMREF |
+				V4L2_VC1_PICTURE_LAYER_FLAG_REFFIELD))) {
+		forward_vb2 = NULL;
+		backward_vb2 = NULL;
+		fwd_interlaced = interlaced;
+	} else {
+		forward_vb2 = picture->forward_ref_ts ?
+			vb2_find_buffer(vq, picture->forward_ref_ts) : NULL;
+		backward_vb2 = picture->backward_ref_ts ?
+			vb2_find_buffer(vq, picture->backward_ref_ts) : NULL;
+	}
 
 	cedrus_engine_enable(ctx);
 
-- 
